1. AIJ pedestrian-wind benchmark data
-------------------------------------

Publisher:  Architectural Institute of Japan (AIJ)
Source:     https://www.aij.or.jp/jpn/publish/cfdguide/index_e.htm
Reference:  Tominaga, Mochida, Yoshie, Kataoka, Nozu, Yoshikawa & Shirasawa (2008),
            "AIJ guidelines for practical applications of CFD to pedestrian wind
            environment around buildings", J. Wind Eng. Ind. Aerodyn. 96(10-11),
            1749-1761.

The wind-tunnel measurements and geometry definitions published by AIJ for the
guideline benchmark cases are used here as validation targets. Case A measurements
are the split-film data of Meng & Hibi (1998) as distributed by AIJ.

Derived files in this repository (converted from the AIJ workbooks by the scripts
in scripts/, with the source URL, SHA-256 and retrieval date recorded inside each
file so the derivation can be reproduced and audited):

