2. Lid-driven cavity reference data
-----------------------------------

Reference:  Ghia, U., Ghia, K.N. & Shin, C.T. (1982), "High-Re solutions for
            incompressible flow using the Navier-Stokes equations and a multigrid
            method", J. Comput. Phys. 48, 387-411.

Tabulated centerline velocity values from that paper (Re=100 and Re=1000 columns)
are reproduced in packages/core/src/fixtures/ghia.ts as validation targets, with
provenance notes in docs/handoff/H9-fixtures-ghia.md.


3. Algorithms
-------------

All solver algorithms are implemented from published literature, not ported from
other implementations. In particular the in-place streaming scheme follows
Lehmann, M. (2022), "Esoteric Pull and Esoteric Push: Two Simple In-Place
Streaming Schemes for the Lattice Boltzmann Method on GPUs", Computation 10(6):92
(MDPI, CC BY 4.0). No code from FluidX3D or any other non-permissively licensed
solver has been read, fetched or ported — see the clean-room rule in CLAUDE.md.
